  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation under RBC-TOC-02 for 5 patients. Each has a progress note, plus an addendum note wherever a late arrival changed a decision.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg BID (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum. Potassium chloride stopped (mr-00076). Pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution, so home omeprazole kept and pantoprazole not ordered. Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged. Lisinopril was first kept on hold because K was 5.4 on 10/21, and I created task-t0003. A repeat BMP on 10/23 (doc-00901) then showed K 4.7 and SCr 1.21, so lisinopril 10 mg (mr-00072) was resumed. Task-t0003 is now obsolete, but the system would not let me cancel it from the inbox: please close it. An unsigned draft addendum (furosemide 60 mg BID, doc-00902) was not acted on.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): Carvedilol was first raised to 12.5 mg BID per the discharge summary. A signed addendum arrived (doc-00904) reversing the increase for bradycardia, so it is back to 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0016). Net: no change from his home dose. Aspirin and insulin 70/30 unchanged. Flagged to you:\n- Atorvastatin 80 mg: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. No change made (comm-t0006).\n- Glipizide 5 mg from an outside prescriber (Dr. Desai): no clinic order, and the discharge papers don't mention it. Not ordered (comm-t0007).\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): Lisinopril 20 mg was resumed on the 10/22 BMP (SCr 1.08, K 4.6). A potassium of 5.5 then arrived on 10/23 (obs-09002), so it is back on hold (mr-00373). Task-t0018 is with you, due 10/26, for the repeat potassium. Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge SCr 1.12 and K 4.4 on 10/21. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. The discharge summary also called for a potassium 3 days after discharge, which has not resulted yet.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): Metformin ER is still on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in hospital before discharge, and the condition requires post-discharge labs. Task-t0013 is with you, due 10/24, for the post-discharge BMP. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nAll 4 inbox items that arrived during the work were reviewed and closed.",
